#!/bin/sh
# The program Chromium starts for `com.omahouse.meter` — docs/design.md §5.2.
#
# Three lines, and it is a shim on purpose. A native messaging manifest names one
# executable and Chromium runs it with the calling extension's origin as the only
# argument, so it cannot name `omahouse meter`; and docs/design.md §3 says there
# is one binary and the daemon is a verb of it, not a second program. This is how
# both hold: the host is a verb of `omahouse`, and this is what turns an argv
# Chromium chose into that verb.
#
# It runs as whoever opened the browser — `.temp/spike-extension.md` §1 measured
# uid 1001, in the child's own session — and asks for nothing.
exec /usr/bin/omahouse meter "$@"
